[en.PIHC_WS_C05_desc]
Discord today is still chaotic, joking as he always did, but with a different purpose. Once, he joked because it was his nature; now, he jokes to cover his guilt. There is no doubt that Discord has done it wrong. In the Ultimate Battle, he lost his magic, and he lost the pony that meant the world to him.\n\nBut as a draconequus who has spent thousands of years in or as a stone statue, Discord’s mentality is much more stable than that of the ponies. Discord fled to the Everfree Forest, where he and Zecora organized a force that could hardly be called an “army”: a draconequus without magic, a rhyming zebra, a few ponies who escaped from Ponyville, a flock of cockatrices, two bears, a lion, a hydra, two pigs, a sea serpent, and a lot of cardboard...\n\nIn the days of the Everfree Forest, aided by the Kingdom of Thicket, they played hide and seek with the Empire’s patrol, Discord learned potion-making from Zecora, and Zecora learned about magic and spells from Discord — although they both don’t know how to cast spells now.\n\nIn the winter of 1000, Zecora decided to return to the Farasi to support the zebra’s resistance against the Changelings. Discord extended his forces to the Hayseed Swamps, continued to organize his forest animal army and sheltering more ponies who escaped from Ponyville or other areas of Equestria. As the Empire’s army was trapped in the snowstorm of the Crystal Empire, Discord began to attack, and through potion-making and the magic of the various relics in the Everfree Forest, his unorganized army successfully drove the Empire’s army out of the Everfree Forest.\nIn the spring of 1001, under the guidance of the “Forest Surrounds Town” doctrine, Discord’s army successfully became a trouble that the Empire could not handle. Discord contacted Starlight Glimmer and Sunset Shimmer, putting the Empire in a dilemma of fighting on two fronts. Unfortunately, they still failed to overthrow the Empire, and Discord retreated to the Hayseed Swamps to recuperate, deepening his alliance with King Aspen.\nAlthough they are far from overthrowing the Empire, at least they have stuck to the Empire like gum on the sole of a shoe.

[en.C05_DESC]


